<reference id="dita-subset" audience="author">
  <title>Supported DITA subset</title>
  <shortdesc><keyword keyref="product-name"/> parses a documented subset of DITA 1.3 itself, in
    TypeScript, with no Java toolchain. Every element it supports is listed here.</shortdesc>
  <refbody>
    <section id="how-elements-are-matched">
      <title>How elements are matched</title>
      <p>Elements are matched by name. DTDs are not fetched or applied, so a <codeph>DOCTYPE</codeph>
        line is fine but has no effect, and <codeph>@class</codeph> specialisation is not used. Common
        HTML character entities such as <codeph>&amp;nbsp;</codeph>, <codeph>&amp;mdash;</codeph>,
        <codeph>&amp;rarr;</codeph> and <codeph>&amp;trade;</codeph> are understood without a DTD.</p>
      <p>An element outside the subset still renders, as a plain block, and validation reports it as an
        <codeph>unsupported-element</codeph> warning.</p>
    </section>

