    <section id="map-elements">
      <title>Map and bookmap elements</title>
      <p>Maps may contain <codeph>map</codeph>, <codeph>bookmap</codeph>, <codeph>title</codeph>,
        <codeph>topicmeta</codeph>, <codeph>navtitle</codeph>, <codeph>linktext</codeph>,
        <codeph>shortdesc</codeph>, <codeph>keywords</codeph>, <codeph>keyword</codeph>,
        <codeph>searchtitle</codeph>, <codeph>data</codeph>, <codeph>topicref</codeph>,
        <codeph>topichead</codeph>, <codeph>topicgroup</codeph>, <codeph>keydef</codeph>,
        <codeph>mapref</codeph>, <codeph>ditavalref</codeph>, <codeph>anchor</codeph>,
        <codeph>anchorref</codeph>, <codeph>navref</codeph>, <codeph>chapter</codeph>, <codeph>part</codeph>,
        <codeph>appendix</codeph>, <codeph>appendices</codeph>, <codeph>frontmatter</codeph>,
        <codeph>backmatter</codeph>, <codeph>notices</codeph>, <codeph>booktitle</codeph>,
        <codeph>mainbooktitle</codeph>, <codeph>booktitlealt</codeph>, <codeph>bookmeta</codeph>,
        <codeph>booklists</codeph>, <codeph>toc</codeph>, <codeph>indexlist</codeph>,
        <codeph>glossarylist</codeph>, <codeph>tablelist</codeph>, <codeph>figurelist</codeph>,
        <codeph>reltable</codeph>, <codeph>relheader</codeph>, <codeph>relcolspec</codeph>,
        <codeph>relrow</codeph>, <codeph>relcell</codeph>, <codeph>glossref</codeph> and
        <codeph>resourceid</codeph>.</p>
      <p>Of these, navigation is built from <codeph>topicref</codeph>, <codeph>topichead</codeph>,
        <codeph>topicgroup</codeph>, <codeph>mapref</codeph>, <codeph>chapter</codeph>,
        <codeph>part</codeph>, <codeph>appendix</codeph>, <codeph>frontmatter</codeph> and
        <codeph>backmatter</codeph>; keys come from any element with <codeph>keys</codeph>. Relationship
        tables, <codeph>anchor</codeph>, <codeph>navref</codeph>, <codeph>ditavalref</codeph> and the book
        lists are accepted and ignored. See <xref href="topics-and-maps.dita"/>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="not-supported">
      <title>Not supported yet</title>
      <ul>
        <li>DTD processing and <codeph>@class</codeph> specialisation.</li>
        <li><codeph>conrefend</codeph> ranges and <codeph>conaction</codeph>. They produce an
          <codeph>unsupported-conref</codeph> warning, and only the start element is pulled.</li>
        <li>Relationship tables, key scopes and branch filtering with <codeph>ditavalref</codeph>.</li>
        <li>Topic references to external or non-DITA resources (<codeph>unsupported-topicref</codeph>).</li>
        <li>DITAVAL flagging styles: <codeph>flag</codeph> includes the content without styling it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </refbody>
